Z||000000||BigTurbo87GT||04-17-2001||09:52 AM||||Can anyone tell me the dimensions of the flywheel in a V6 fiero.<BR>Looking for outer diameter, thickness, teeth, pilot bushing diameter.<BR>I need to reproduce a custom flywheel that will match the Getrag.<BR>Is there any other specs I need?<BR>Thanks for any input.<BR>Bill||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||04-17-2001||03:10 PM||||I don't know the specs but, other than the balancing weight, it's the same flywheel that sits in any 90 - 97 5-spd GM (3.1, 3.4, etc).  Keep in mind you'll have to get your new one balanced for the Fiero V6 (the other GM's are neutral).  If you're not concerned about balancing at this stage, pick up a used GM flywheel from the wreckers (I bought a '97 neutrally balanced flywheel for my Fiero's bored-out 2.8 to 3.1 for $30 CDN with about 15000 miles on it).||||reg||1
Z||000002||BigTurbo87GT||04-17-2001||03:15 PM||||Thanks for the additional info But,<BR>the problem is this flywheel will have a Northstar motor on the other side of it.<BR>The machinest needs to know the dimensions in order to create the flywheel. They have the Northstar crank pattern, I need to supply the rest.<BR>||||reg||1
